-- d3b_refinement_safety_transfer: the REFINEMENT verdict PAYOFF — property
-- transfer along a step-simulation, authored in CLEAN's surface language and
-- checked by CLEAN's CIC kernel (so it enters the clean kernel's trust base).
--
-- d3 (step_simulation) proves step-simulation => reachability inclusion:
--   Reach C InitC StepC c  ->  Reach A InitA StepA (f c).
-- That is necessary but not yet USEFUL: what a refinement verdict is FOR is to
-- discharge a concrete safety property by proving it on the (simpler) abstract
-- system. This file closes that loop — the composition of d3 with the safety
-- inductive-invariant principle (tB / reach_least):
--
-- SOUNDNESS CLAIM (proved below, `refinement_safety_transfer`). Given a
-- step-simulation `f : C -> A` (hInit + hSim, exactly as in d3) AND an abstract
-- predicate `J : A -> Prop` that is an INDUCTIVE INVARIANT of the abstract
-- system (contains the abstract initial states, closed under abstract steps),
-- every C-reachable concrete state `c` satisfies `J` at its image:
--     Reach C InitC StepC c  ->  J (f c).
-- i.e. an abstract invariant pulls back along the refinement map to a concrete
-- invariant. This is the property-transfer that justifies checking a property
-- on the abstract model and concluding it for the concrete one.
--
-- PROOF. Direct induction on the concrete reachability derivation (`Reach.rec`,
-- the SAME `Reach` as tB / e3 / d3), carrying `J (f s)` as the motive:
--   base : InitC s --(hInit)--> InitA (f s) --(hJinit)--> J (f s).
--   step : concrete StepC s t with IH `J (f s)`; (hSim) gives
--            StepA (f s) (f t) \/ f s = f t, cased by Or.rec:
--              inl (genuine abstract step): (hJstep) closes J from (f s) to (f t);
--              inr (stutter f s = f t):     transport IH : J (f s) along the
--                                           equality to J (f t) via Eq.subst.
-- (Equivalently: d3 gives Reach A (f c), then reach_least on J closes it. The
-- direct induction fuses the two so the file is self-contained — each .clean is
-- checked in a fresh `with_prelude` env and cannot cite the other files.)
--
-- FULLY GENERAL: arbitrary state types C, A, arbitrary Init/Step relations, an
-- arbitrary refinement map f, and an arbitrary abstract invariant J.

-- The reachability predicate of a transition system (identical to tB / e3 / d3):
inductive Reach (State : Type) (Init : State -> Prop) (Next : State -> State -> Prop) : State -> Prop where
  | base : (s : State) -> Init s -> Reach State Init Next s
  | step : (s : State) -> (t : State) -> Reach State Init Next s -> Next s t -> Reach State Init Next t

theorem refinement_safety_transfer
    (C : Type) (A : Type)
    (InitC : C -> Prop) (InitA : A -> Prop)
    (StepC : C -> C -> Prop) (StepA : A -> A -> Prop)
    (f : C -> A)
    -- step-simulation (as in d3):
    (hInit : (c : C) -> InitC c -> InitA (f c))
    (hSim : (c : C) -> (c' : C) -> StepC c c' -> Or (StepA (f c) (f c')) (@Eq A (f c) (f c')))
    -- J is an inductive invariant of the ABSTRACT system:
    (J : A -> Prop)
    (hJinit : (a : A) -> InitA a -> J a)
    (hJstep : (a : A) -> (a' : A) -> J a -> StepA a a' -> J a')
    -- conclusion: every concrete-reachable state's image satisfies J
    (c : C) (h : Reach C InitC StepC c) : J (f c) :=
  @Reach.rec C InitC StepC
    -- motive: the image of every reachable concrete state satisfies J
    (fun s _hs => J (f s))
    -- base: InitC s --(hInit)--> InitA (f s) --(hJinit)--> J (f s)
    (fun s hi => hJinit (f s) (hInit s hi))
    -- step: concrete StepC s t, IH `J (f s)`; case the simulation on (f s),(f t)
    (fun s t _hr hn ih =>
      @Or.rec (StepA (f s) (f t)) (@Eq A (f s) (f t))
        (fun _ => J (f t))
        -- inl: a genuine abstract step (f s) -> (f t); J is closed under StepA
        (fun hstepA => hJstep (f s) (f t) ih hstepA)
        -- inr: stutter f s = f t; transport IH : J (f s) along the equality
        (fun heq => @Eq.subst A (fun z => J z) (f s) (f t) heq ih)
        (hSim s t hn))
    c h
